    How to Build and Setup the Kernel:
            --Prerequisites--
        Build host: Linux or Windows 11 + WSL2.

        On Debian/Ubuntu/WSL, install the normal build tools:
            sudo apt install clang lld nasm make xorriso git mtools

        For disk-image testing with a populated MINIX v1 filesystem,
        install mkfs.minix too:
            sudo apt install util-linux

        For running in QEMU:
            sudo apt install qemu-system-x86

        Or install Windows QEMU and set QEMU to the executable path before
        running scripts\run-qemu.ps1 from PowerShell.

            --Standard workflow--
        From the repository root:
            make doctor             # checks required and optional tools
            make bootstrap-limine   # clones/builds boot/limine once
            make                    # builds build/kernel.elf and build/kernel.iso
            make run                # boots the ISO in QEMU

        The default build uses native JNU userspace and does not require
        musl. Musl is optional and only used by make musltest / make iso-musl.
        To build musl: clone into user/musl, configure with prefix=install
        and --disable-shared, then make install — see docs/source/musl.rst.

    Makefile Targets:
        make help        : Shows the supported build interface.
        make doctor      : Checks host tools and Limine setup.
        make bootstrap-limine: Clones/builds Limine into boot/limine.
        make             : Builds native userspace, kernel ELF, initramfs, ISO.
        make kernel      : Builds build/kernel.elf.
        make user        : Builds native user/*/main.c programs.
        make iso         : Builds build/kernel.iso.
        make musltest    : Builds optional build/user/bin/musltest.
        make iso-musl    : Builds build/kernel-musl.iso including musltest.
        make font        : Regenerates the generated font header under build/.
        make ata-disk    : Creates build/disk.img. Default is 32 MiB
                           (override with SIZE=N). Uses mkfs.minix when present.
        make run         : Boots in QEMU and attaches build/disk.img if it exists.
        make run-disk    : Creates/requires build/disk.img and boots with it.
        make debug       : Boots QEMU paused (-s -S), ready for GDB attach.
        make debug-disk  : Debug boot with the ATA disk image attached.
        make vmware-disk : Builds disk.img and converts to disk.vmdk for VMware.
        make docs        : Builds Sphinx HTML docs.
        make clean       : Removes reproducible build artifacts but keeps disk.img.
        make clean-disk  : Wipes build artifacts and disk.img.
        make distclean   : Also removes boot/limine.

        See docs/source/build.rst for the same setup contract in the manual.

    Running on VMware:
        JNU needs a MINIX v1 disk on legacy IDE 0:0 (hda). A blank disk
        from the VMware wizard has no filesystem and will panic with
        "invalid magic 0x0000" at mount — this is not caused by guest RAM.

            make ata-disk       # or: make vmware-disk for a .vmdk
            # VM settings: IDE bus, IDE 0:0, attach build/disk.img or disk.vmdk

        See docs/source/build.rst ("Running on VMware") for full steps.

